+// The web sidecar runs Next.js in server output mode on Linux (config/index.ts
+// forces "server"), so the packaged web package's next.config.ts is re-loaded at
+// runtime. Its module scope computes WORKSPACE_ROOT as the grandparent of the
+// installed web package (node_modules/) and reads the CMS host-release
+// fingerprint inputs at <WORKSPACE_ROOT>/apps/web/... and
+// <WORKSPACE_ROOT>/packages/contracts/... — a layout that only exists in the
+// build workspace, not inside an assembled package. Mirror those exact files to
+// the paths the config computes so the config loads instead of crashing the web
+// sidecar (and with it the whole packaged boot). Content is irrelevant: the
+// build-time fingerprint embedded in .next is authoritative; only the reads
+// must succeed.
